direction: right
title: Authentication vs Authorization (Airport Model)

AuthN: Authentication (AuthN): "Who are you?" {
  style.fill: "#06201B"
  style.stroke: "#10B981"
  checkpoint: "TSA Checkpoint: Passport & Biometrics"
  outcome: "Identity confirmed: 'You are John Doe'"
  status: "Failure: 401 Unauthorized"
}

AuthZ: Authorization (AuthZ): "What are you permitted to do?" {
  style.fill: "#1C1917"
  style.stroke: "#F59E0B"
  gate: "Gate Agent: Flight 402, Seat 12B allowed"
  lounge: "VIP Lounge: Economy ticket denied"
  status: "Failure: 403 Forbidden"
}

AuthN -> AuthZ: Authenticated identity passed to authorization manager { style.stroke: "#38BDF8" }
